WEBVTT

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.890
Racing isn't to go fast. Go faster. Push car and driver to the edge. Beyond.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:26.980
Team Fast X won the first NASCAR Unlimited Series championship.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.880
But this is a new season, a new challenge.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.140
That's why we created the XPT Racers.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.730
Fastest cars in the world, and the best drivers in the world.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:51.910
Carlos Stuntz Ray, Steve Flyer Sharp, Megan Spitfire Faster,

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.170
last year's NASCAR Unlimited Series Driving Champion,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.540
Mark Charger McCutcheon.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:13.560
Do you have time for a quick interview? Well, I've always got time for an interview. What's Charger McCutcheon really like?

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.750
Sorry no time

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.400
Nascar has given Rexcore a second chance to be part of the Unlimited series.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.320
What do you intend to do differently this season?

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.410
I intend to win.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:58.620
Driver puts the fast in Fast X.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:02:59.700
More!

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:42.810
First seen before on the track and they're headed in the wrong chin.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.100
Chick.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.530
The drivers are out of their cars and on the track.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:07.070
Are you local?

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.770
You're going in the wrong direction.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.450
We go our own way.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.740
Meet your new competition.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:13.940
Yeah?

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.360
So who are you anyway?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:16.970
They call me Redline.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.130
That's Chrome, Octane, and Grim Reaper.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.360
And I'm Tank.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.140
It's the idea of coming onto the track like that.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.660
We're looking for a race.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.960
If you're not afraid to drive against somebody else...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.160
you haven't already beaten.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.140
Frayed!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.160
Easy, Charlie.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.750
We're on TV, man.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.900
We're not here to race.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.800
We're just demonstrating the new cars.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.950
They're chicken, Redline.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:45.460
Everybody knows that's why Flyer quit the Air Force.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:46.520
What?

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:47.900
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.680
Settle down, you guys!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:59.470
Is this a private party, or can anybody join in?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:05:59.870
Hey.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:04.320
Redline, maybe Rexcar has the backbone to race us.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:10.180
I'm having more backbone in my little finger than Fastex is having in its cold feet.

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:13.550
Come on, we'll race Rexcar.

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.360
We're not just going to sit here and watch him race Rexcar.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.500
What do you say, Megan?

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:23.780
I say we need about an hour to prep the cars for a race.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:26.060
Ha ha! Let's get charged!

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.160
One hour, baby.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.610
Let's get this show on the road.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:55.990
It's only one hour to get ready, Carlos.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:59.970
Not enough time to repair your car or even get a back

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:05.770
car ready. I need to be in this race, Jack. This is my chance to show what I can do. If we work on

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:11.490
your car, we won't have time to prep the other three. We have to set priorities. Yeah, and it's

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:16.140
easy to see who's the numero uno priority. Charger earned that attention by winning the

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:22.000
championship. You've got another chance to win this year. Yeah, maybe I'd have a better chance

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:29.330
if I was driving for another team. Let's get those carbs adjusted, the tires set up.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.340
Can you tape those grills for me, kid?

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:32.830
You bet, duck!

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.580
I'm gonna hang around if I can't race.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.420
That's it, chiquita.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.940
You need an autograph or something?

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.970
Come on, come here.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.980
Oh, but you can.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.100
Chargers autograph?

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:02.400
Agh!

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:04.660
Hey!

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.170
These people need pit passes.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.120
guests of Team FastX.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:10.720
Okay.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.220
Do you tell Charger if he doesn't give you an autograph?

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.180
I'll kick his bumper.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.900
You can't keep me out.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:18.620
Hey man, I'm Lalo and...

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:19.230
Collector!

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.150
I used to drive for Rexco.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.310
Sorry, fella. Your name's not on the list.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.390
care what it says on the list!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.500
I'm not watching the race in the stands!

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:29.980
I belong on a...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.420
TRACK!

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:31.590
I'm a driver.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.640
sure you'd be coming back.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:52.840
Hey, I'm a member of this team, Jack.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.260
What can I do to help?

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.560
Everything's really crazy with the new season starting up.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.500
With all the interviews, and public appearances, and fans, I don't know.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:04.970
I feel like everything's out of control.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.060
Like I'm in a spin.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.280
But it all straightens out again when I think about what you said at the end of last season.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:12.760
Good.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.990
feel the same way I do.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.060
about you.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:20.100
You two look like you're discussing race strategy.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.100
How about sharing it with our viewers?

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:24.650
Uh, I, uh...

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:25.540
Oh!

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:27.910
We're just changing this oil pump.

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:29.100
And I'm helping.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:29.910
Oof!

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:42.400
Char-McCutcheon, last year's driving champion.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:43.720
This is a restroom!

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:45.730
Have a moment's peace?

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:47.710
AHH!

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:50.010
Are you hurt, Charger?

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:54.710
And if you are, do you think it'll affect your chances to repeat as the Unlimited Series champion?

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:58.180
I'm having enough of seeing Charger's rear bumper!

00:09:58.900 --> 00:09:59.420
AHHHHH!

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:08.820
Red line.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:28.280
You see

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:29.930
I never get.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:30.380
picked.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.160
Hey, don't worry.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.380
When I was your age,

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:33.800
I didn't get picked either.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.160
and ready to go.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:57.460
And they're off.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:00.852
Thank you.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:25.970
I'm out.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:31.090
Yes.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:31.680
Thank you.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:42.740
My name's Gooch.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.460
But my friends call me Lugnut.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.830
It's no use, Jack. I'm going out to the pits.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:54.030
Whoa!

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.240
I've been hearing about these new atomic fuel cars.

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.050
Don't touch anything! These engines are complicated!

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:10.520
Hey, if you wanna know about Fleece, you ask the dog here.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.230
Oh, yeah! I'm back!

00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:15.860
You want a job?

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.950
Unlimited Champion Charger McCutcheon

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:40.700
Thank you.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.600
party, Serena, or can anybody join in?

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:36.300
She's a private race, baby, and that means anything goes.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:06.180
What happens when you're wearing this thing down?

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:09.780
AHH!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:10.220
OH!

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:11.430
Oh.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:12.800
That's what happens.

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.850
I'm charging McCutcheon is back in the race.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:31.880
Stop.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:32.750
Yeah.

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:34.940
Come on.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:13.340
Spitfire?

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:14.240
I'm all right.

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.540
And nobody really calls me Spitfire, okay?

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:18.710
should.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.030
suits you.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.260
Are you all right, Megan?

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.310
She looks fine to me.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:35.390
I'm dark.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:36.970
Feels like the suspension.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:38.870
is headed for the fence.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:40.600
That looks serious!

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.410
You're running a great race, Carlos. Even if we can't get you back out...

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:49.780
LOGNUT! Suspension!

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:50.940
Sure thing, Doc!

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:56.620
Couldn't have found out what's wrong that fast!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:57.980
Found it! Fixed it!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.330
Fire it up!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.000
It was the finish line.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:13.920
The race is back in the race.

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:15.930
I want to be a winner.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:17.280
I got to earn it.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:47.340
belongs to

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:48.630
Reign

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:04.100
Great race, Stunts.

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:05.420
Outstanding.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:07.600
Thanks, guys. Gracias.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.340
You drove like a real champion, amigo.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.320
Hey, but it doesn't even count.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.340
No championship points and no prize money.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:18.130
Not even a pretty girl with a kiss for the winner.

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:19.780
Next time, Stunts.

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:27.290
Man, even when I win, I can't win.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.220
I got your autograph.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:35.720
Thank you.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:38.550
stunts.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:40.180
Can we have an interview, please?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:42.760
I've always got time for an interview.
